lection signal"], "rationale": "With no polls, ratings, or markets to weigh, the forecast rests on California's durable Democratic lean, which points to a double-digit margin; the active Democratic primary fight does little to alter the general-election picture.", "watch": "Early general-election polling or a sharp shift in the national environment could move the margin in either direction.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "California enters the 2028 presidential race as one of the most Democratic-leaning states in the country, and with the Republican incumbent term-limited, both major parties will nominate new candidates. The state's durable partisan lean points to a double-digit Democratic margin in the general election.\n\nDirect evidence remains scarce: no general-election polls, expert ratings, or market pricing are available yet, and coverage so far centers on a crowded Democratic primary featuring Gavin Newsom, Kamala Harris and other contenders. The primary outcome is unlikely to change the state's underlying lean, so the forecast holds near fundamentals with wide uncertainty. A stronger-than-expected Republican nominee or a shifted national climate could narrow the gap, but the fundamentals give Democrats a clear edge.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9157, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8615, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8622, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8596, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.8693, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8671, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8635, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.8619, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.